ssed in H1 due to debarment and lower certification delays; targeting 30-35% in new sectors (aviation, metros); cost control maintained via low attrition (3-4%) and in-house talent pool; USD-denominated international contracts improve margin resilience","src":"concall","as_of":"Q2FY26"},"capital_allocation":{"title":"Capital allocation","body":"Reinvestment in talent acquisition, digital capabilities (BIM/AI), and international business development; no dividends or buybacks mentioned; focus on organic growth via empanelments and JV partnerships","src":"concall","as_of":"Q2FY26"},"management_tone":{"title":"Management quality / tone","body":"Confident, proactive, and strategically focused; management emphasizes recovery from debarment, sectoral diversification, and digital transformation; tone is optimistic on Q3/Q4 performance and international pipeline","src":"concall","as_of":"Q2FY26"},"risks":{"title":"Risks & watch-items","body":"Dependence on government payments (though 100% guaranteed); slow international project conversion cycles (2-year lead time); bid win rate currently low at 1% abroad (targeting 5-10%); potential delays in land acquisition affecting certification and cash flow","src":"concall","as_of":"Q2FY26"},"non_obvious":{"title":"Non-obvious takeaways","body":"Despite 90% order book from NHAI, management is actively reducing dependency by targeting state governments with higher margins; international revenue potential is underappreciated — Mozambique project already delivered, with Ghana/Zambia in advanced talks; BIM/AI adoption is not just efficiency play but a competitive moat for winning larger global tenders","src":"concall","as_of":"Q2FY26"},"challenges":{"title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers","body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| NHAI debarment caused 40% revenue drop in Q2FY26 | DHRUV | beneficiary | High | Debarment lifted in July 2025; recent empanelments and bid wins confirm recovery |\n| Low international bid win rate (1%) | DHRUV | beneficiary | Medium | Targeting 5-10% win rate; Africa pipeline is active and JV model is proven |","src":"concall","as_of":"Q2FY26"}}}